    },
    "message": "Answer history while a save is being indexed\n\nA save moves the branch pointer before it indexes the new head, so history\nsearches, checkpoint pages and conversation tails in between failed with\nhistory_index_stale. They now answer as of the index's own head, which\nanswering_head() also gives nearest(). History and checkpoint pages name\nthat head in anchor_hash and indexed_through_minute, and their cursors bind\nto it. A history search reads one index transaction, so a pointer moving\nduring it no longer fails it with history_changed_during_query.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
